  "review_notes": [
    "Independently reviewed the actual top-level proposal.json in full, not merely the proposal embedded in context.prior_result. Also read functionality.md, both disposition ledgers through exhaustion, coverage.json and unresolved.json.",
    "The single proposed write targets the owned ftPe_AttackS4_Enter state_behavior fact. Canonical source, consecutive enum definitions, HSD_Randi implementation, OnDeath reset, transition declaration and animation helper support its bounds, ordering, arguments and qualifications. No additional write is necessary for acceptance.",
    "The current ledgers specifically defer the broad previous-use, command-clearing and friction-reduction claims that the earlier librarian packet retained. This independent review agrees with those deferrals; acceptance does not promote unresolved claims.",
    "All 20 baseline outgoing records were compared against the exact links ledger. Their relationships remain supported by canonical callback bodies, the active Peach motion table and the common AttackS4 caller. Historical duplicate records remain separate; no merge or new relationship is authorized.",
    "Canonical ftAnim_8006EBA4 and ft_80084104 were checked against their definitions. Rendered ftAnim_Advance and ft_CheckGroundAndFall were not used as proof.",
    "Boundary review confirms three inclusive candidates, acceptance of the first candidate for an out-of-range saved ID, exclusion of the saved in-range ID, shared RNG advancement on rejected attempts, and reset-scoped rather than unlimited historical nonrepetition. No exact equiprobability or worst-case retry bound is promoted.",
    "Optional physics and completion branches, signed zero, NaN and infinities were checked at the inspected comparison sites. Final movement and predicate contracts remain deferred. Source establishes no local allocation, release, pointer retention or captured callback state; scheduler and downstream lifetime guarantees remain deferred.",
    "Nonblocking documentation issue: the first local callback citation in functionality.md's animation section has a mistyped revision. The document explicitly supplies the correct canonical citation near its end, and proposal.json and the disposition ledgers use the correct revision. The valid citation is code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/src/melee/ft/kinds/ftPeach/ftpeachattacks4.c#L35-L40.",
    "The animation-section phrase 'No qualifying successful test returns false' is read as absence of a successful qualifying test causing the query to return false, including an empty scan. Canonical ftAnim_IsFramesRemaining unambiguously returns true upon any qualifying successful test and false after exhausting the scan.",
    "Review identity: /root/review_gate/kernel/reviewer-main__melee__ft__kinds__ftPeach__ftpeachattacks4-1."
  ],
